# ERP Asset Management

Policy: [docs/architecture/erp-asset-management.md](docs/architecture/erp-asset-management.md)

**Option B is locked.** Asset Management is a separate module from Finance. When a table exists, Asset is a Shared Registration Master — not a required parent of Machine or Vehicle.

```text
Machine  = Maintenance operational master
Vehicle  = Transport operational master
Asset    = Shared registration (Phase 1 live: `assets`, `/assets`)
Finance  = Expense today; Financial Profile later — never a second asset register
```

## Phase 2 opened for Maintenance PM (order 2026-10-22, Maintenance Phase 3.5)

- `Machine.assetId?` and `TransportVehicle.assetId?` exist: optional, unique, `SetNull`. Link one row at a time from the asset page; same company and branch; audit every change.
- `Asset.maintenancePmEnabled` is the switch "เข้าแผนซ่อมบำรุง". Only active assets not `RETIRED`/`DISPOSED`. Separate from the QR PM (`AssetPmPlan`).
- `MaintenancePlan` / `MaintenanceSchedule` / `WorkOrder` carry `assetId?`; `machineId` is optional with a CHECK that one of them is set. New plans target an asset; legacy machine-only rows still work.
- A failed check on any asset (vehicles too) opens a corrective WO in Maintenance. Never create `TransportRepairLog` from Maintenance; do not edit `repair-service.ts`.
- Transport reads WO status only: assignment is refused while the linked asset has a WO `in_progress`/`on_hold`. Maintenance never writes `TransportVehicle.currentStatus`.

## Do not create (until an explicit order with a first use case)

- `FixedAsset`, `ITAsset`, `FinanceAsset`, `GLAsset`, `AccountingAsset`
- `MaintenanceAsset`, `TransportAsset`, `AssetVehicle`, `ProductionAsset`
- VehicleProfile / MachineProfile tables that duplicate existing columns
- Auto-backfill or auto-create of assets from machines/vehicles (still forbidden after Phase 2)
- Location master, Component tree, Custodian, Transfer, depreciation engine — because of Asset
- Finance Expense rows from Maintenance (Finance Phase 4 is locked)

## Leave as-is

- `Machine` stays Maintenance. Work orders keep `machineId` (filled from the linked asset when present).
- `TransportVehicle` stays Transport. Jobs / GPS / tire / repair keep `vehicleId`.
- Nav department `asset_management` still means Machines — it is not a register.
- `ExpenseTransactionType.ASSET` is an expense classification, not a register.
- `machine-asset-service.ts` is machine media / BOM, not Asset.
- Finance cost objects stay type + label (Phase 4 locked). Do not require Asset ids.

## Before adding any asset-like table

1. Is this identity (register), operational profile, or financial valuation?
2. Does Machine / Vehicle / SparePart already own this meaning?
3. Is there an explicit Phase 1+ order plus a first use case (IT register or company capitalization)?

Anything beyond the Phase 2 scope above (more FKs, backfill, FA engine) needs a new human order.

See also [erp-shared-master.mdc](erp-shared-master.mdc) and [finance-expense-ssot.mdc](finance-expense-ssot.mdc).
